# The vendored ZK JavaScript must round-trip byte-for-byte.
#
# `crates/viche-frontend/public/vendor/VENDOR.md` publishes a SHA-256 for every
# file in that directory, and `make frontend-vendor-check` recomputes them. With
# git's default text handling plus `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default),
# a fresh clone would materialise those files with CRLF line endings, every
# hash would differ from the published one, and the audit trail — the entire
# point of vendoring code that handles voters' secrets — would be worthless.
#
# `-text` disables both eol conversion and any newline normalisation on commit.
crates/viche-frontend/public/vendor/** -text

# Same reasoning, smaller stakes: the ZK artifacts are binary.
*.wasm binary
*.zkey binary
*.ptau binary
*.r1cs binary
*.wtns binary
